# Subagent worktrees are full copies of this repo (git worktree add). Left in
# the scan corpus, every source file exists 7+ times, graphify's near-duplicate
# detection collapses them, and a worktree copy can win — evicting the real file
# and shrinking the corpus to almost nothing. That is what silently broke
# `graphify update` here (diagnosed 2026-07-21): rebuilds produced 59 nodes
# against an existing 793-node graph, and the fail-closed guard refused to write.
.claude/worktrees/

# Scratch/vendor trees that are not this project's source.
web/node_modules/
web/.next/

# pytest writes .pytest_cache/.gitignore containing a bare "*". graphify
# accumulates every walked directory ignore file into ONE global pattern list,
# so that "*" leaked out and ignored the entire repo — detect() returned 0 files
# and every `graphify update` rebuilt a 59-node graph that the fail-closed guard
# (correctly) refused to write over the real 793-node one. Diagnosed 2026-07-21.
.pytest_cache/

# Same bare "*" leak as .pytest_cache (see above).
.superpowers/sdd/

# Same bare "*" pattern — added preemptively, these tools all write one.
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
htmlcov/
.tox/
